d Aerojet acquisition; goodwill-heavy\n   balance sheet; Aerojet segment margins still low (12.3% vs peers).\n   Not yet proven. 1/3\n3. Capex efficiency: historic capex exceptionally low (2% revenue);\n   guided step-up to ~$600M FY2026 and ~$1.5B FY2028 for capacity.\n   Unproven. 1/3\n4. Mix rationality: returning ~60% of FCF (buybacks + dividends) while\n   delevering; sensible. 2/3\n5. Guidance accuracy: raised guidance 2x in FY2026; beat consensus 4\n   consecutive quarters [Actual]. 3/3\nCapital allocation score: 9/15.\nInsider ownership: 0.42% [Actual] \u2014 low. No recent insider transaction\ndata [Unconfirmed]. Score: 0 (no bonus; no penalty).\n\nSECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\nStep 2.5-1 R&D Capitalization:\nR&D not separately disclosed in the data pack. Company commentary cites\n\"increased research and development costs\" as a margin offset [Actual].\nEstimate: ~$900M\u2013$1.2B annual (4\u20135% of revenue) [Assumption, secondary].\nCap at 4-year amortization: adj. NOPAT adds back ~$700\u2013900M net after\namortization [Assumption].\n\nStep 2.5-2 SBC Treatment:\nSBC = $0.113B in FY2025 (ending Jan-2026) [Actual \u2014 pack Section 5].\nAdjusted FCF: $2.682B \u2212 $0.113B = $2.569B (-4.2%) [Arithmetic].\nSBC is minor \u2014 no distortion.\n\nStep 2.5-3 Operating Lease Capitalization:\nOperating leases: $0.785B [Actual]. Add to net debt \u2192 adj. net debt\n~$10.85B. Coverage still adequate. Immaterial.\n\nStep 2.5-5 Adjusted ROIC:\nAdjusted NOPAT = GAAP NOPAT $1.96B + after-tax R&D net $0.80B = $2.76B\n[Estimate]. Adjusted IC = $29.7B + unamortized R&D $2.5B + leases $0.8B =\n$33.0B [Estimate]. Adjusted ROIC \u2248 8.4%. Still below WACC, though\ntangible-asset ROIC is far higher (self-funded IC excluded). GAAP ROIC\nis depressed by ~$20B+ goodwill; the underlying business is compounding.\n\nStep 2.5-6 Owner Earnings:\nFY2025 (ending Jan-2026): NI $1.606B + D&A $1.224B \u2212 maintenance capex\n$0.42B \u2212 \u0394WC $0.782B = $1.63B