ndustry converts\nat ~$0. Working-capital swings modeled as zero in steady state.\nFlagged as modeling judgment.\n\nStep 3-D: PV Calculation (WACC 7.7%):\nPV explicit FCFFs (years 1\u201310):\n3.39/1.077=3.15; 3.76/1.160=3.24; 3.83/1.249=3.07; 4.00/1.346=2.97;\n4.23/1.449=2.92; 4.11/1.561=2.63; 4.19/1.681=2.49; 4.29/1.810=2.37;\n4.39/1.950=2.25; 4.50/2.100=2.14\n\u03a3 = $27.23B [Arithmetic]\nPV(TV) = 88.7 / 2.100 = $42.2B [Arithmetic]\nEV = $69.4B; Equity = 69.4 \u2212 10.0 = $59.4B\nBase intrinsic value = $59.4B / 186.156M = $319.1/share [Arithmetic]\n\nSensitivity \u2014 IV/share to key assumptions:\n| Scenario variant | IV/share |\n|------------------|----------|\n| FY2029\u201335 growth 1% instead of 3% | ~$270 |\n| FY2029\u201335 growth 5% instead of 3% | ~$375 |\n| Terminal margin 12.0% instead of 13.2% | ~$290 |\n| Terminal margin 14.5% | ~$350 |\n| WACC 7.3% | ~$355 |\n| WACC 8.2% | ~$280 |\n| Capex FY2028 $1.0B (not $1.5B) | ~$330 |\n| OCF FY2028 $4.5B (not $5.0B) | ~$300 |\nRange: $270\u2013375 across plausible single-variable moves. Base $319.\n\nStep 3-E: Multiples Cross-Check:\n- Trailing P/E: TTM EPS $10.07 \u2192 26.5x [Arithmetic; vendor 29.1x\n  definitional difference]\n- Forward P/E (FY2026 EPS $11.90 mid): 22.4x [Arithmetic]\n- Forward P/E (FY2027 est. EPS $13.30, consensus growth 11.9%):\n  20.1x [Estimate]\n- EV/EBITDA (FY2026): $59.7B / (2.63+1.25) = 15.4x [Arithmetic]\n- Peer comparison: defense primes trade ~17\u201320x forward EPS; LHX at\n  20x FY2027 is at parity-to-premium, justified by 7\u20138% organic growth\n  vs. peers 3\u20135% [Assumption from sector knowedge \u2014 peer P/Es not\n  retrievable before budget limit]\n- PEG (forward): 20.1 / 11.9 = 1.69 [Arithmetic] \u2014 above 1, not cheap\n- Dividend yield: 1.75% [Actual \u2014 vendor]\nConclusion: DCF ($319) sits above the current price ($267); multiples\nsuggest the stock is fair-to-modestly-undervalued if growth delivers.\nCross-checks agree: NOT a deep value; an above-average-quality franchise\nat a reasonable price.\n\nReverse DCF at $266.73:\nCurrent price implies ~3.5% revenue CAGR post-FY2028 with 12% margins \u2014\nbelow my base (3\u20134% growth + 13.2% margin). The market is pricing the\ndefense-budget normalization more harshly than the company framework\nand my base case. Feasible \u2014 not excessive.\n\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\nCompetitive response: Defense is a relational oligopoly; LHX success in\nprogram wins (Golden Dome, NOVA, NGJ) does not trigger price wars \u2014 rival\nprimes win other programs. Impact: \u22121 (neutral-to-slight negative from\nprogram-by-program competition).\nReflexivity: stock down 30% YTD has NOT impaired franchise (security-\ncleared contract commitments dominate; SBC dilution is minor at $113M/yr).\nPositive reflexivity: buybacks at lower prices increase per-share value.\nCustomer behavioral shift: DoD moving from just-in-case to wartime-footing\nprocurement \u2192 favorable for backlog conversion and accelerated awards.\nLTV/CAC not applicable (non-transactional).\n\nSECTION 4. SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\nStep 4-1/4-2 Scenario probabilities (total = 100%):\n- BEAR (20%): Defense budget normalization severe; FY2027 reconciliation\n  partially clawed back; FY2028 real spend \u221220%. Revenue $23.4B (FY2026),\n  $24.1B (+3%), $24.8B (+3%), then +2%. EBIT margin 11.5%\u219212.0%; OCF\n  stalls at $3.9B by FY2028. WACC 8.2%; terminal g 2.0%.\n  IV \u2248 $185/share.\n- BASE (50%): Company hits FY2026 guidance and FY2028 framework; budget\n  normalization moderate; OCF/FCF compound; margins expand. IV = $319.\n- BULL (30%): Defense supercycle sustains via $1.5T FY2027 request and\n  elevated base thereafter; international demand accelerates; LHX\n  execution beats framework. Revenue FY2028 $28.0B, FY2030 $32.5B; OCF\n  FY2028 $5.5B; margin 14.2% by FY2030. WACC 7.5%; terminal g 2.75%.\n  IV \u2248 $450/share.\n\nStep 4-3 Bayesian update:\nPrior based on base rates: P(>5% 5-yr revenue CAGR