0\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 7.5. CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n- The portfolio's common bear trigger: US federal fiscal consolidation\n  (sequestration 2.0) knocks down ALL defense positions simultaneously.\n  Correlation of LHX with LMT/NOC/RTX during sector stress: ~0.85\u20130.95.\n  [Estimate]\n- Tail correlation (2008/2020/2022 pattern): defense behaves like the\n  market in fast drawdowns (\u03b2 ~0.8\u20131.0) despite low 1-yr beta 0.746.\n- Conditional VaR (weekly CVaR 5%): if defense sector de-rates 15% on a\n  budget shock, LHX expected 1-month loss \u2248 \u221212% to \u221215%. [Assumption]\n- Mitigation: cap aggregate defense-prime exposure at 20% of the book;\n  pair with TIPS or cash if fiscal-expansion trade is crowded.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 8. MONITORING RULES\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nStep 7-1. Thesis integrity thresholds (KPI dashboard \u2014 quarterly)\n1. Book-to-bill \u2265 1.0 (Q1 1.4x, Q2 1.2x). RE-EVALUATE if <0.90 for two\n   consecutive quarters.\n2. Backlog \u2265 $40B (current $42B record). RE-EVALUATE if <$35B (backlog\n   erosion >15%).\n3. GAAP operating margin \u2265 10.5% (Q2 11.1%). RE-EVALUATE if <10.0%.\n4. Segment operating margin \u2265 16.0%. RE-EVALUATE if <15.0%.\n5. FY26 FCF \u2265 $2.9B (guide ~$3.0B). RE-EVALUATE if <$2.5B.\n6. Net debt < $10.0B by end-FY27. RE-EVALUATE if >$11.5B.\n7. Missile Solutions IPO: re-file by Q2 2027; DoW $1B anchor intact.\n   RE-EVALUATE if cancelled/announced as permanent spin.\n8. FY27 defense appropriation \u2265 +15% vs FY26. RE-EVALUATE if <+10%.\n9. Golden Dome follow-on awards \u2265 $1B cumulative by end-2027.\n\nStep 7-4. Pre-mortem \u2014 \"It is January 2031. LHX is down 65%. Why?\"\n1. The defense fiscal cliff: FY2028\u20132030 budgets reverted to +3%/yr after\n   the FY27 surge; backlog shrank; P/E de-rated to 15x \u2192 $110. Early\n   warning: book-to-bill <0.9; appropriations lag; sequestration chatter.\n2. Missile Solutions stayed inside LHX; Aerojet propulsion cost overruns\n   resurfaced (fixed-price missile contracts overrun); FCF fell to $1.5B;\n   debt stayed >$10B \u2192 $135. Early warning: DoW $1B anchor withdrawn or\n   IPO cancelled outright; quarterly FCF miss; cost-overrun disclosures.\n3. Space execution failure: Golden Dome satellites failed acceptance;\n   SDA canceled follow-on tranches; goodwill/intangibles impaired; margin\n   compression to 6% \u2192 $95. Early warning: launch failures, schedule\n   slips, negative SDA milestone news, fixed-price loss provisions.\n\nStep 7-5. (see Section 11 Decision Journal)\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u25