: NI $1.606B + D&A $1.224B \u2212 maintenance capex\n$0.42B \u2212 \u0394WC $0.782B = $1.63B [Arithmetic]. FY2026 (guided basis): NI\n~$2.23B + D&A ~$1.25B \u2212 capex $0.60B \u2212 \u0394WC ~$0 = ~$2.88B [Estimate].\n\nSECTION 3. VALUATION \u2014 ENGINE 1 (DCF + MULTIPLES)\n\nStep 0-1/0-2: Enterprise Archetype = B (Quality Compounder, in transition\nfrom D). Valuation Engine = Engine 1 (DCF + Multiples), with a blend of\nEngine 2 discipline (normalizing the FY2028 budget cliff).\nStep 0-3 Transition analysis: LHX exhibits 50\u201380% of criteria for\nOption-Led \u2192 Quality (core revenue >50% organically, segment GM >30%,\npositive FCF for 2+ years). Transitioning from D \u2192 B. Blended approach:\nDCF primarily; multiples as cross-check. Conviction \u22120.5 for transition\nuncertainty (already embedded).\n\nStep 3-A: Discount-Rate Derivation:\n- Risk-free rate: 4.71% (10Y UST) [Actual \u2014 TradingEconomics 2026-08-21]\n- Equity risk premium: 4.75% [Assumption \u2014 long-run US ERP]\n- Beta: 0.80 [Assumption \u2014 blend of vendor beta 0.746 and fundamental\n  peers ~0.8; defense is low-beta]\n- Cost of equity: 4.71 + 0.80 \u00d7 4.75 = 8.51% [Arithmetic]\n- Pre-tax cost of debt: 4.8% [Assumption \u2014 A-/BBB+ credit, 10Y + ~60bps]\n- Tax rate: 17% [Estimate \u2014 GAAP ETR FY2025 16.9%; YTD FY2026 14.4%;\n  normalized 17%]\n- After-tax cost of debt: 3.98% [Arithmetic]\n- Capital structure: E = $49.65B / (49.65+10.05) = 83.2%; D = 16.8%\n- WACC = 0.832 \u00d7 8.51% + 0.168 \u00d7 3.98% = 7.75% \u2192 ROUND 7.7% [Assumption]\n\nStep 3-B: Explicit Forecast \u2014 Revenue, Margins, OCF, Capex, FCFF:\nFiscal years end early January. All values [$B].\n\n| FY | Rev | EBIT% | EBIT | OCF | AT Int | Capex | FCFF |\n|----|-----|-------|------|-----|--------|-------|------|\n| 2026 | 23.45 | 11.2% | 2.63 | 3.60 | 0.39 | 0.60 | 3.39 |\n| 2027 | 25.10 | 11.8% | 2.89 | 4.20 | 0.36 | 0.80 | 3.76 |\n| 2028 | 27.00 | 12.5% | 3.38 | 5.00 | 0.33 | 1.50 | 3.83 |\n| 2029 | 28.22 | 13.0% | 3.67 | 4.70 | 0.30 | 1.00 | 4.00 |\n| 2030 | 29.35 | 13.2% | 3.87 | 4.90 | 0.28 | 0.95 | 4.23 |\n| 2031 | 30.23 | 13.2% | 3.99 | 5.05 | 0.26 | 1.20 | 4.11 |\n| 2032 | 31.14 | 13.2% | 4.11 | 5.20 | 0.24 | 1.25 | 4.19 |\n| 2033 | 32.07 | 13.2% | 4.23 | 5.35 | 0.22 | 1.28 | 4.29 |\n| 2034 | 33.03 | 13.2% | 4.36 | 5.51 | 0.20 | 1.32 | 4.39 |\n| 2035 | 34.02 | 13.2% | 4.49 | 5.68 | 0.18 | 1.36 | 4.50 |\n\nSourcing of drivers:\n- FY2026 revenue = company guidance midpoint $23.2\u201323.7B [Actual]\n- FY2027 revenue = $25.1B interpolation to FY2028 framework [Assumption]\n- FY2028 revenue = company framework $27.0B [Actual \u2014 press release]\n- FY2029\u201335 revenue = decel to 4%, 4%, 3%, 3%, 3%, 3%, 3% [Assumption \u2014\n  NOT guided; based on CSIS defense-budget normalization (FY2028 real \u221216%,\n  then flat real ~2% nominal), plus backlog conversion. I explicitly note\n  this path is assumption-driven and test sensitivity below.]\n- EBIT margins: FY2026 = H1 actual 11.2% [Actual]; FY2027\u201328 = segment\n  margin path 16.0 \u2192 16.5% with 4.0\u20134.5pp corporate drag narrowing\n  [Assumption]; FY2030+ = 13.2% terminal (segment ~17% less ~3.8pp drag)\n  [Assumption]\n- OCF: FY2026 = guidance [$Actual]; FY2028 = company framework $5.0B\n  [Actual]; others interpolated/scaled [Assumption]\n- Capex: FY2026 = guidance; FY2028 = framework-implied $1.5B; others\n  smoothed [Assumption]\n- AT interest: FY2026 ~$0.39B on ~$10.8B avg debt at 4.5% pre-tax\n  [Estimate]; declines as debt amortizes [Assumption]\n\nStep 3-C: Terminal Value:\nTerminal FCFF = FY2035 FCFF $4.50B, growing at 2.5% (nominal GDP proxy;\ndefense budget stabilizes) [Assumption]. Implied terminal FCF margin\n= 13.2%, in line with NOPAT margin = sustainable with zero net\nreinvestment (price-led growth).\nTV = 4.50 \u00d7 1.025 / (0.077 \u2212 0.025) = $88.7B [Arithmetic]\nROIC check: Terminal reinvestment = 2.5/10 = 25% of NOPAT would reduce\nFCFF to ~$2.5B \u2014 however, the company requires no net fixed-capital for\ninflation-led revenue growth; working capital in this industry converts\nat ~$0. Working-capital swings modeled as zero in steady state.\nFlagged as modeling judgment.\n\nStep 3-D: PV Calculation (WACC 7.7%):\nPV explicit FCFFs (years 1\u201310):\n3.39/1.077=3.15; 3.76/1.160=3.24; 3.83/1.249=3.07; 4.00/1.346=2.97;\n4.23/1.449=2.92; 4.11/1.561=2.63; 4.19/1.681=2.49; 4.29/1.810=2.37;\n4.39/1.950=2.25; 4.50/2.100=2.14\n\u03a3 = $27.23B [Arithmetic]\nPV(TV) = 88.7 / 2.100 = $42.2B [Arithmetic]\nEV = $69.4B; Equity = 69.4 \u2212 10.0 = $59.4B\nBase intrinsic value = $59.4B / 186.156M = $319.1/share [Arithmetic]\n\nSensitivity \u2014 IV/share to key assumptions:\n| Scenario variant | IV/share |\n|------------------|----------|\n| FY2029\u201335 growth 1% instead of 3% | ~$270 |\n| FY2029\u201335 growth 5% instead of 3% | ~$375 |\n| Terminal margin 12.0% instead of 13.2% | ~$290 |\n| Terminal margin 14.5% | ~$350 |\n| WACC 7.3% | ~$355 |\n| WACC 8.2% | ~$280 |\n| Capex FY2028 $1.0B (not $1.5B) | ~$330 |\n| OCF FY2028 $4.5B (not $5.0B) | ~$300 |\nRange: $270\u2013375 across plausible single-variable moves. Base $319.\n\nStep 3-E: Multiples Cross-Check:\n- Trailing P/E: TTM EPS $10.07 \u2192 26.5x [Arithmetic; vendor 29.1x\n  definitional difference]\n- Forward P/E (FY2026 EPS $11.90 mid): 22.4x [Arithmetic]\n- Forward P/E (FY2027 est. EPS $13.30, consensus growth 11.9%):\n  20.1x [Estimate]\n- EV/EBITDA (FY2026): $59.7B / (2.63+1.25) = 15.4x [Arithmetic]\n- Peer comparison: defense primes trade ~17\u201320x forward EPS; LHX at\n  20x FY2027 is at parity-to-premium, justified by 7\u20138% organic growth\n  vs. peers 3\u20135% [Assumption from sector knowedge \u2014 peer P/Es not\n  retrievable before budget limit]\n- PEG (forward): 20.1 / 11.9 = 1.69 [Arithmetic] \u2014 above 1, not cheap\n- Dividend yield: 1.75% [Actual \u2014 vendor]\nConclusion: DCF ($319) sits above the current price ($267); multiples\nsuggest the stock is fair-to-modestly-undervalued if growth delivers.\nCross-checks agree: NOT a deep value; an above-average-quality franchise\nat a reasonable price.\n\nReverse DCF at $266.73:\nCurrent price implies ~3.5% revenue CAGR post-FY2028 with 12% margins \u2014\nbelow my base (3\u20134% growth + 13.2% margin). The market is pricing the\ndefense-budget normalization more harshly than the company framework\nand my base case. Feasible \u2014 not excessive.\n\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\nCompetitive response: Defense is a relational oligopoly; LHX success in\nprogram wins (Golden Dome, NOVA, NGJ) does not trigger price wars \u2014 rival\nprimes win other programs. Impact: \u22121 (neutral-to-slight negative from\nprogram-by-program competition).\nReflexivity: stock down 30% YTD has NOT impaired franchise (security-\ncleared contract commitments dominate; SBC dilution is minor at $113M/yr).\nPositive reflexivity: buybacks at lower prices increase per-share value.\nCustomer behavioral shift: DoD moving from just-in-case to wartime-footing\nprocurement \u2192 favorable for backlog conversion and accelerated awards.\nLTV/CAC not applicable (non-transactional).\n\nSECTION 4. SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\nStep 4-1/4-2 Scenario probabilities (total = 100%):\n- BEAR (20%): Defense budget normalization severe; FY2027 reconciliation\n  partially clawed back; FY2028 real spend \u221220%. Revenue $23.4B (FY2026),\n  $24.1B (+3%), $24.8B (+3%), then +2%. EBIT margin 11.5%\u219212.0%; OCF\n  stalls at $3.9B by FY2028. WACC 8.2%; terminal g 2.0%.\n  IV \u2248 $185/share.\n- BASE (50%): Company hits FY2026 guidance and FY2028 framework; budget\n  normalization moderate; OCF/FCF compound; margins expand. IV = $319.\n- BULL (30%): Defense supercycle sustains via $1.5T FY2027 request and\n  elevated base thereafter; international demand accelerates; LHX\n  execution beats framework. Revenue FY2028 $28.0B, FY2030 $32.5B; OCF\n  FY2028 $5.5B; margin 14.2% by FY2030. WACC 7.5%; terminal g 2.75%.\n  IV \u2248 