n <10.0%\n  \u2022 FY27 defense appropriation <+15% (downgrade to HOLD, not exit)\n  \u2022 DoW $1B anchor withdrawn from Missile Solutions (exit)\n  \u2022 Net debt >$11.5B without IPO progress (downgrade)\n\nRATIONALE IN ONE PARAGRAPH: L3Harris is a wide-moat defense electronics\nprime selling at 22.4x FY26 adjusted EPS near its 52-week low because the\nmarket has punished the Missile Solutions IPO delay and refuses to pay\nfor margin expansion. The data (record $42B backlog, book-to-bill 1.2x,\ntwo guidance raises, Q2 EPS beat) and the regime (+44% FY27 defense\nbudget request) contradict the market's stagnation assumption. At $266.73\nthe price embeds a ~5.5\u20136% FCF CAGR; my base case is ~10% with an\namortization wind-down and margin-path to 12% by 2030. The bear case\n(budget normalization, permanent IPO failure) is real but is adequately\ncompensated at a 15.1% margin of safety. Position size is deliberately\ncapped at 7% because ROIC remains below WACC and the deleveraging\ncatalyst has slipped to 2027\u20132029.\n\n\u2500\u2500 END OF REPORT \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n```"}, {"sample": 3, "iv": 260.0, "plausible": true, "reasons": [], "flags": [], "truncated": false, "secs": 477, "report": "```markdown\nSECTION 0 \u2014 ANALYSIS OVERVIEW\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Ticker:** LHX |