es FY29\u201330 revenue growth of 4%/yr \u2014 that is \u2264 sector base rate, not >1.5\u00d7 the base rate. No red flag. But my assumed terminal FCF growth (2.5%) \u2248 long-run nominal GDP \u2014 consistent with the base rate for a mature defense prime. No re-evaluation needed.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2 \u2014 BUSINESS QUALITY ASSESSMENT\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 2-1. Business understanding (3 sentences):**\nL3Harris supplies defense electronics, space payloads/satellites, secure communications, and missile/rocket-motor systems to the US DoD, allied governments, and (increasingly) the new Department of War, operating through three segments: Space & Mission Systems, Communication & Spectrum Dominance, and Missile Solutions. The business model is contract-based (long-duration programs, 28% classified) with record backlog of ~$42B providing high revenue visibility. It is mid-transition: management is spinning off Missile Solutions (Axyv), selling space propulsion, and refocusing on \"Trusted Disruptor\" growth areas.\n\n**Understandability:** Medium (defense contracts are complex; classified work opaque). No downgrade \u2014 segment-level metrics disclosed.\n\n**Step 2-2. Moat assessment (0\u20133 each):**\n| Moat type | Score | Moat direction |\n|---|---|---|\n| Intangible assets (brand, IP) | 2 | Stable |\n| Switching costs | 3 | Widening (installed base of 1M+ software-defined radios; 20% planned expansion) |\n| Network effects | 0 | N/A |\n| Cost advantage | 2 | Stable (revenue/employee +25% over 2 yrs) |\n| Economies of scale | 2 | Stable |\n| Regulatory barriers | 3 | Widening (ITAR, clearances, DoW co-investment) |\n| Data moat | 1 | Widening (classified ISR, space data) |\n| **Total** | **13/21** | **Wide moat, direction stable-to-widening** |\n\n**Step 2-3. Lynch classification:** **Cyclical** (defense budget cycle) with **Fast-Grower** momentum in the current up-leg. Key checkpoints for cyclicals: (a) cycle position \u2014 recent peak; (b) inventory/backlog \u2014 backlog record; (c) normalized earnings power \u2014 mid-cycle GAAP EPS $9.50\u201311.00 [Assumption].\n\n**Step 2-4. Financial strength scorecard:**\n- Revenue growth: FY23\u2192FY25 CAGR = \u221a(21.325/19.419) \u2212 1 = **+4.8%** [Arithmetic]; FY26E +10% (7% organic) [Actual guidance]\n- GAAP operating margin: FY25 = 9.0%; FY26E TTM = 9.4%; 8-yr median 16.6% [Pack \u2014 Arithmetic]; segment op margin 16.0% [Actual \u2014 Q2'26]\n- EPS growth: FY25 $7.88 \u2192 FY26E $11.90 = **+51%** [Actual guidance vs Arithmetic]\n- ROE: TTM NI/equity = 1.606/19.635 = **8.2%** [Arithmetic]\n- ROIC: ~6\u20137% GAAP; ~10% ex-acquisition amortization [Estimate]\n- FCF margin: 2.682/22.39 = **12.0%** [Arithmetic]; FCF conversion of OCF \u2248 86% [Arithmetic]\n- Net debt/EBITDA \u2248 11.06/3.36 \u2248 **3.3\u00d7** [Arithmetic/Estimate]; interest coverage \u2248 2.11/0.50 \u2248 **4.2\u00d7** [Estimate \u2014 interest expense FY26 not in pack]\n- Structure: Net debt $11.06B including op leases; $1.82B maturing by Jan 2027 [Estimate \u2014 ts2.tech]\n\n**Judgment:** **Adequate-to-Good.** Leverage is the weak point (3.3\u00d7 vs defense-prime norm ~2\u00d7); FCF conversion is the strong point.\n\n**Step 2-5. Capital allocation scorecard (0\u201315):**\n1. Buyback efficiency: net issuance \u22121.2% (1-yr) but 3-yr CAGR +4.8% (net issuance \u2014 pack); purchases at $300\u2013380 [Estimate] seen at high multiples \u2192 **1/3**\n2. M&A track record: Aerojet RD (2023) added debt and integration risk; segment margins only now expanding after 10 quarters \u2192 **1/3**\n3. Capex efficiency: capex/revenue only ~2% (governments fund facilities), incremental ROIC not directly measurable but guided FCF margin high \u2192 **2/3**\n4. Rationality of mix: portfolio simplification (Missile IPO, space propulsion sale), debt paydown, modest dividend (1.75%) \u2192 **2/3**\n5. Guidance accuracy: raised FY26 EPS twice, but revenue midpoint below consensus at Q2; FY25 revenue guide had been reduced earlier \u2192 **1/3**\nInsider bonus: insider ownership 0.42% (<5%); no cluster buying observed \u2192 0.\n**Total: 7/15.**\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2.5 \u2014 INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 2.5-1. R&D capitalization:**\nR&D \u2248 2.5\u20133% of revenue (~$0.6B FY26E) + $1B customer-funded R&D [Actual \u2014 company transcript Q1'26]. If capitalized over 4 years (straight-line), adjusted OI = 2.11 + (0.60 \u2212 0.60\u00d70.25\u00d72) \u2248 +$0.30B; adjusted IC = 41.2 + ~$1.2B unamortized. Adjusted ROIC \u2248 (2.11+0.30)/(41.2+1.2) = **5.8%** [Arithmetic/Assumption]. Still below WACC.\n\n**Step 2.5-2. SBC treatment:**\nSBC FY26 TTM = $0.113B [Actual \u2014 pack]. Adjusted FCF = 3.0 \u2212 0.113 = **$2.89B** [Arithmetic]. SBC is 0.5% of revenue \u2014 small; no material impact.\n\n**Step 2.5-3. Operating lease capitalization:**\nOperating leases $0.785B [Actual]. Adjusted net debt = 11.347 + 0.785 \u2212 1.069 = **$11.063B** [Arithmetic]. Adjusted EBITDA \u2248 3.36 + 0.10 implied lease interest [Estimate] \u2248 $3.46B; net debt/EBITDA \u2248 **3.2\u00d7**.\n\n**Step 2.5-4. Brand/data assets:** Not quantified \u2014 no methodology available for defense intangibles beyond regulatory moat. [Unconfirmed]\n\n**Step 2.5-5. Adjusted ROIC:** \u2248 5.8\u20136.5% GAAP; ex-amortization \u2248 10% [Estimate]. Gap >5pp driven by amortization from L3\u2013Harris merger and Aerojet acquisition \u2014 a real but non-cash cost.\n\n**Step 2.5-6. Owner Earnings (Buffett):**\nOwnerE = NI $1.606B + D&A $1.224B \u2212 maintenance capex (~$0.35B [Assumption]) \u2212 \u0394WC (\u2212$0.782B = working capital released) + SBC $0.113B \u2248 **$3.38B** [Arithmetic/Assumption]. Strong conversion, boosted by a one-time WC release \u2014 not all repeatable.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3 \u2014 VALUATION (ENGINE 2: CYCLE-ADJUSTED)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 3-1. Cycle position: PEAK.** US defense base budget $1.1T + $350B reconciliation (FY26) and ~$1.5T request (FY27) are records; FY28 projected \u221216% real [Estimate \u2014 Defense Aerospace]. LHX revenue FY26E = $23.45B (+10%); FCF $3.0B guidance near all-time high.\n\n**Step 3-2. Discount-rate derivation (WACC):**\n| Component | Value | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Risk-free rate (Rf) | 4.71% | [Actual \u2014 10Y UST, Aug 21, 2026, TradingEconomics] |\n| Equity risk premium | 4.75% | [Assumption \u2014 Damodaran-style long-run implied ERP] |\n| Beta (used) | 0.90 | [Assumption \u2014 vendor beta is 0.746 but window/benchmark unknown; defense group de-rates in selloffs; stand-alone gap risk high] |\n| Cost of equity | 4.71 + 0.90\u00d74.75 = **8.99%** | [Arithmetic] |\n| Pre-tax cost of debt | 4.80% | [Estimate \u2014 10Y UST + ~10bps credit spread; LHX BBB-ish] |\n| After-tax cost of debt (21%) | 3.79% | [Arithmetic] |\n| Weights (E: 49.65 / 60.16; D: 11.35 / 60.16) | 82.5% / 17.5% | [Arithmetic \u2014 using market cap + debt incl. fin leases] |\n| **WACC** | **0.825\u00d78.99 + 0.175\u00d73.79 = 8.08% \u2248 8.0%** | [Arithmetic/Assumption] |\n\nSensitivity: if vendor beta 0.746 were used, WACC = 7.4% and IV rises ~20% (see tornado).\n\n**Step 3-3. Explicit forecast (base case; FY26E is guided/filed):**\n\n| Fiscal year | Revenue ($B) | Growth | Segment op margin | OCF ($B) | Capex ($B) | FCF ($B) | D&A ($B) | Sources |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| FY25 (actual) | 21.325 | \u2014 | ~15.7% [Est] | 2.559 | 0.408 | 2.151 | 1.289 | [Actual \u2014 pack] |\n| FY26E | 23.45 | +10% (7% organic) | 16.0% (guided low-16) | 3.45 | 0.45 | 3.00 | 1.25 | [Actual guidance: $23.2\u201323.7B rev, $3.0B FCF; capex Estimate from FY25 run-rate] |\n| FY27E | 24.86 | +6% | 16.3% | 3.70 | 0.55 | 3.15 | 1.25 | [Estimate: FY27 budget up ~20%, Golden Dome $17.5B request, MAC orders; capex up for munitions/space capacity] |\n| FY28E | 24.36 | \u22122% | 16.5% | 3.60 | 0.50 | 3.10 | 1.25 | [Estimate: defense budget \u221216% real; LHX protected by intl + classified + backlog; revenue \u22122% net] |\n| FY29E | 25.09 | +3% | 16.8% | 3.80 | 0.50 | 3.30 | 1.20 | [Estimate: recovery, space/comms re-accelerate; intl +6%] |\n| FY30E | 26.09 | +4% | 17.0% | 4.10 | 0.60 | 3.50 | 1.15 | [Estimate: LHX share gains in space/munitions; intl +8%] |\n\n**Beyond FY30 (terminal):** FCF = $3.6B, growth = 2.5% [Assumption \u2014 not established by any company guidance; defense grows at ~nominal GDP long-run. If you assume 0% growth: IV \u221217%; if 3.5%: IV +12%.]\n\n**Step 3-4. Discounted cash flow (base case, $B):**\nPV(FY26E FCF) = 3.00/1.080 = 2.78\nPV(FY27E FCF) = 3.15/1.166 = 2.70\nPV(FY28E FCF) = 3.10/1.260 = 2.46\nPV(FY29E FCF) = 3.30/1.360 = 2.43\nPV(FY30E FCF) = 3.50/1.469 = 2.38\n**PV explicit = $12.75**\nTerminal value = 3.60\u00d71.025/(0.080\u22120.025) = $67.1; PV = 67.1/1.469 = **$45.7**\nEnterprise value = 12.75 + 45.7 = **$58.5B**\nLess: net debt $10.278B (LT+current+fin leases \u2212 cash) [Arithmetic]\nLess: operating leases $0.785B [Arithmetic]\n**Equity value = $47.4B \u2192 $254.6 per share** (\u00f7 186.16M shares)\n\n**Step 3-5. Cross-check \u2014 normalized multiples:**\n- Mid-cycle GAAP EPS: $9.50\u2013$11.00 [Assumption]. At 18\u201320\u00d7 (defense-normal multiple): **$171\u2013$220**.\n- FY26E EV/EBITDA: EBITDA \u2248 3.45 [Estimate]; market EV = $59.9B \u2192 17.4\u00d7. Mid-cycle multiple 13\u201315\u00d7: **$185\u2013$223**.\n- FCF yield on my IV: 3.0/58.5 EV = 5.1% \u2014 reasonable for the risk.\nThe multiple cross-check is 15\u201325% below the DCF \u2014 this is the classic explicit-growth gap. The DCF is my primary model because it captures the FY27 up-year and FY28\u201330 recovery explicitly.\n\n**Step 3-6. Tornado sensitivity (Top 3 variables):**\n| Variable | \u22121\u03c3 | Base | +1\u03c3 | IV range |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| WACC | 8.5% | 8.0% | 7.4% | ~$212 \u2194 ~$300 |\n| FY30 terminal FCF | $3.2B | $3.6B | $4.0B | ~$238 \u2194 ~$278 |\n| FY28 revenue growth | \u22126% | \u22122% | +2% | ~$242 \u2194 ~$267 |\n\n**Base intrinsic value after cross-check reconciliation: \u2248 $255** [Estimate]. Blend with WACC uncertainty toward the median: **$245\u2013$265 range**.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3.5 \u2014 SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 3.5-1. Competitive response:** If LHX succeeds in munitions/space, RTX, NOC, LMT, and Leonardo DRS will bid aggressively for the same budget dollars. Counter-move impact: **\u22121** (moderate). In defense prime land, budget share is zero-sum; LHX's 16% segment margin expansion invites price competition on future competitions.\n\n**Step 3.5-2. Reflexivity:** Positive reflexivity exists: higher stock price \u2192 SBC attracts engineering talent, M&A currency for consolidation (Axyv IPO would enable Axyv to raise capital independently). Negative reflexivity risk: if the stock stays at $267, the postponed Axyv IPO may be delayed further and the DoW may demand harsher terms on the $1B investment. Net: **mildly positive reflexivity during the IPO cycle**.\n\n**Step 3.5-3. Customer behavior evolution:** DoD is shifting from \"best-value\" to \"speed and scale\" procurement (multiyear authorities, MAC, Golden Dome). This favors LHX's missile/space franchises but erodes the moat of legacy \"custom-built\" defense electronics (commoditization of radios). LTV/CAC not applicable to a contract business; backlog per dollar of revenue is the best proxy \u2014 currently 2\u00d7 revenue, record.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 4 \u2014 SCENARIO ENGINE (BAYESIAN)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 4-2. Scenario composition (probabilities sum to 100):**\n\n| Scenario | Probability | Key assumptions | IV | Price in 3 yrs |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Bear** | **25%** | H2 FY26 FCF miss (only ~$2.2B delivered of $3.0B guidance); FY28 budget decline \u221216% real hits LHX with \u22126% revenue; Missile IPO delayed past FY28; segment margin rolls over to 14.5%; leverage 3.5\u00d7 | $185 | ~$175 [Estimate] |\n| **Base** | **50%** | Guidance delivered; FY27 +6%; FY28 \u22122%; margins expand to 17%; IPO completes FY27 with deleveraging; FCF terminal $3.6B | $255 | ~$260 [Estimate] |\n| **Bull** | **25%** | All of base, plus MAC $25B orders convert and accelerate; Golden Dome front-loads; segment margin 17.5% by FY28; intl mix >30%; Axyv IPO unlocks $8\u201310B value, proceeds cut debt to <2\u00d7; terminal FCF $4.5B | $320 | ~$330 [Estimate] |\n\nExpected IV = 0.25\u00d7185 + 0.50\u00d7255 + 0.25\u00d7320 = **$254** [Arithmetic]\nExpected 3-yr price = 0.25\u00d7175 + 0.50\u00d7260 + 0.25\u00d7330 = **$256** (+1.75% dividend yield \u2192 ~+2%/yr). [Arithmetic]\n\n**Step 4-3. Bayesian update:**\nPrior (Layer 1.5): defense prime 5-yr survival \u226595%; budget-cycle underperformance 30\u201340%.\nLikelihood evidence:\n- Backlog 2\u00d7 revenue + book-to-bill 1.2 (Q2) and 1.4 (Q1) \u2192 raises success likelihood\n- H1 FCF only $584M vs $3.0B guide \u2192 lowers success likelihood\n- Missile IPO postponed \u2192 lowers value-unlock likelihood\n- 10 straight quarters of segment margin expansion \u2192 raises operational likelihood\nPosterior: bear 25% / base 50% / bull 25% \u2014 reasonably balanced. **I do not deviate >1.5\u00d7 the base rate in the bull case** (success probability 25% vs platform-transition base rate 20\u201330%) \u2192 no red flag.\n\n**Step 4-4/5. Expected price, MoS, CIs:**\n- Expected IV = **$254** [Estimate]\n- 50% CI: **$230\u2013$290**; 80% CI: **$185\u2013$325** [Estimate]\n- MoS = (254 \u2212 266.73)/254 = **\u22125.0% \u2192 None.**\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 4.5 \u2014 TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nMarket-implied horizon at $266.73: my model implies the market is pricing FY28+ earnings power (terminal FCF ~$3.8B \u2014 approximately equal to my FY30\u201331 FCF path). The market is NOT anchored on FY26 peak EPS; it is looking through the cycle.\nSpread vs my 3\u20135 yr horizon: **< 1 year.** No horizon arbitrage exists. The market has already discounted the FY28 budget dip and the FY29\u201330 recovery.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 5 \u2014 CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 5-1. Conviction Score (0\u201315):**\n| Component | Score | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| Business quality | 2/3 | Wide moat, but ROIC \u2248 WACC; cyclical |\n| Valuation attractiveness | 1/3 | Price \u2248 IV; no MoS |\n| Macro alignment | 1/3 | Rates rising; budget cycle rolling over; headwind |\n| Thesis clarity | 2/3 | Clear KPIs (book-to-bill, margins, FCF, IPO) |\n| Execution traceability | 2/3 | Margins expanding 10 straight quarters, but H2 FCF back-loaded |\n| **Total** | **8/15 \u2192 Medium** | \u2014 |\n\nMacro alignment: \u22120.5 steps already included. Conviction decay: \u22121 pt every 6 months without confirming evidence.\n\n**Step 5-3. Sizing guideline:** Medium conviction