each \u2192 re-evaluate):**\n1. **Q3 FY26 FCF < $800M** (implies < $2.0B H2; full-year ~$2.6B or lower) \u2192 downgrade to Bear.\n2. **FY27 revenue guidance < +4%** on the January 2027 call \u2192 downgrade to Bear.\n3. **Segment operating margin < 15.5%** in any quarter \u2192 thesis of margin expansion dead.\n4. **Book-to-bill < 1.0** for 2 consecutive quarters \u2192 backlog cushion no longer growing.\n5. **Missile IPO not re-filed by June 2027** \u2192 Bull case invalid; CapEx discipline at risk.\n6. **10Y UST > 5.25%** \u2192 force re-run of WACC; IV drops ~10%.\n7. **FY28 budget news showing a >20% real decline** \u2192 downgrade to Bear.\n\n**Step 7-4. Pre-mortem (5 years from now, why did LHX fail?):**\n- Scenario A: \"The $3B FCF promise was a mirage.\" H2 FY26 came in at $2.2B, guidance credibility was destroyed, and the stock re-rated to 15\u00d7 trough earnings. Early warning: FCF conversion in Q3/Q4.\n- Scenario B: \"The Budget Cliff won.\" FY28 \u221216% real hit LHX revenue \u22128%; with 3.3\u00d7 leverage, the balance sheet became the bind. Early warning: FY27 guidance as a leading indicator.\n- Scenario C: \"The IPO cannibalized the parent.\" Axyv went public at a high multiple but retained all the growth, leaving LHX as a low-margin comms/space contractor. Early warning: Axyv S-1 registration showing revenue retention <90%.\n\n**Step 7-5. Decision journal entry:** T0 $266.73, IV $254 (50% CI $230\u2013$290), key assumptions: WACC 8.0%, FY28 \u22122%, terminal FCF $3.6B@2.5%, Red Team concern: H2 FCF concentration and FY28 budget transmission.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 9 \u2014 RED T